WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.358 --> 00:00:18.242
Mowgli continued growing and learning the law of the jungle.

2
00:00:18.243 --> 00:00:21.893
One year a terrible drought arrived.

3
00:00:21.894 --> 00:00:28.373
It began when the winter came, bringing little rain.

4
00:00:28.374 --> 00:00:33.667
The yams dried up and few trees flowered.

5
00:00:33.668 --> 00:00:42.007
Next a burning heat crept into the jungle, turning it yellow, brown, and then black.

6
00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:47.607
Water holes turned to mud.

7
00:00:47.608 --> 00:00:56.529
Bamboo stalks grew dry, clanking loudly in the hot wind.

8
00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:01.529
It was the first time that Mowgli had felt deep hunger.

9
00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:06.430
While this hunger was awful, his thirst was worse.

10
00:01:06.431 --> 00:01:14.061
The heat went on and on, drying up all the moisture.

11
00:01:14.062 --> 00:01:19.558
Soon only one river still had water.

12
00:01:19.559 --> 00:01:24.430
Hathi, the wise old elephant, lifted his trunk.

13
00:01:24.431 --> 00:01:29.893
"There is a water truce!" he declared.

14
00:01:29.894 --> 00:01:34.355
Mowgli learned that this meant no one could hunt at the river.

15
00:01:34.356 --> 00:01:39.407
Instead everyone could safely drink there.

16
00:01:39.408 --> 00:01:47.918
The animals whistled and shrieked, spreading the news of the water truce.

17
00:01:47.919 --> 00:01:54.030
"This is a terrible time," Bagheera said one evening at the river.

18
00:01:54.031 --> 00:01:58.852
Mowgli nodded. The air still felt as hot as fire.

19
00:01:58.853 --> 00:02:07.097
Baloo sighed. "The rains have forgotten us this year."

20
00:02:07.098 --> 00:02:11.992
Upstream, Hathi stood with his sons in the moonlight.

21
00:02:11.993 --> 00:02:17.842
Nearby some deer were drinking, along with pigs and wild buffalo.

22
00:02:17.843 --> 00:02:22.128
"The humans are hungry too," a pig said.

23
00:02:22.129 --> 00:02:26.223
"They're dying in their fields."

24
00:02:26.224 --> 00:02:31.979
"Hathi, have you ever seen anything like this drought?" Baloo asked.

25
00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:40.832
"No. But it will pass." Hathi squirted water along his back and sides.

26
00:02:40.833 --> 00:02:43.161
Baloo looked at Mowgli.

27
00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:49.712
"Well, we have someone here who cannot survive much longer without more food.

28
00:02:49.713 --> 00:02:52.931
The boy is all skin and bones."

29
00:02:52.932 --> 00:02:57.198
"Hey!" Mowgli sat up in the water, insulted.

30
00:02:57.199 --> 00:03:01.964
"That's because I don't have any fur to cover my bones."

31
00:03:01.965 --> 00:03:07.692
Everyone laughed, but Mowgli was scowling at Baloo.

32
00:03:07.693 --> 00:03:12.135
"You wouldn't look good without fur either!"

33
00:03:12.136 --> 00:03:19.102
Bagheera put out a paw and gently knocked Mowgli back into the water.

34
00:03:19.103 --> 00:03:23.069
Mowgli rose, spluttering and laughing.

35
00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:27.642
"It's rude to make fun of your teacher, Mowgli," Bagheera said.

36
00:03:27.643 --> 00:03:32.222
Grinning, he dunked Mowgli again.

37
00:03:32.223 --> 00:03:39.092
This time when Mowgli rose from the water, he saw that Bagheera's expression had changed.

38
00:03:39.093 --> 00:03:41.402
"Uh-oh," he thought.

39
00:03:41.403 --> 00:03:47.011
He saw the tiger slinking toward them.

40
00:03:47.012 --> 00:03:53.292
"Why, look at this." Shere Khan's voice was a low rumble.

41
00:03:53.293 --> 00:03:58.892
He bent to take a drink. "It's the man cub."

42
00:03:58.893 --> 00:04:04.761
Mowgli slipped behind Bagheera as Shere Khan dipped his chin in the river.

43
00:04:04.762 --> 00:04:09.920
Soon dark oily streaks were floating in the water.

44
00:04:09.921 --> 00:04:14.219
Bagheera looked suspiciously at the oily streaks.

45
00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.196
"What have you been up to, Shere Khan?"

46
00:04:17.197 --> 00:04:23.344
Shere Khan smiled slyly. "I found a human," he said.

47
00:04:23.345 --> 00:04:30.354
"So I came to the river for a drink—and to clean myself."

48
00:04:30.355 --> 00:04:34.584
A few animals gasped.

49
00:04:34.585 --> 00:04:39.352
"You killed a person during the drought?" Bagheera snapped.

50
00:04:39.353 --> 00:04:42.436
"Couldn't you find something else to eat?"

51
00:04:42.437 --> 00:04:45.726
The tiger just shrugged.

52
00:04:45.727 --> 00:04:51.725
Hathi had been listening quietly.

53
00:04:51.726 --> 00:04:57.345
Now he stepped closer to Shere Khan and swung his trunk.

54
00:04:57.346 --> 00:05:02.995
"As you know, Shere Khan, there is a drought," the elephant said.

55
00:05:02.996 --> 00:05:07.599
"The river is for drinking, not washing off blood.

56
00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:13.209
Besides, we are all suffering—jungle animals and humans.

57
00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:16.954
It is wrong to boast of killing right now."

58
00:05:16.955 --> 00:05:20.130
Shere Khan looked down.

59
00:05:20.131 --> 00:05:23.582
"Have you had enough to drink?" Hathi asked.

60
00:05:23.583 --> 00:05:25.303
"Yes."

61
00:05:25.304 --> 00:05:29.935
"Go then!" Hathi commanded.

62
00:05:29.936 --> 00:05:36.482
His three sons moved to stand behind him.

63
00:05:36.483 --> 00:05:40.897
Shere Khan slunk away, not even daring to growl.

64
00:05:40.898 --> 00:05:46.899
For he knew what everyone knew—Hathi was the master of the jungle.

65
00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:51.048
Bagheera sighed and turned back to Mowgli.

66
00:05:51.049 --> 00:05:53.557
"Never forget this, Little Brother.

67
00:05:53.558 --> 00:06:02.296
Shere Khan is your enemy."
